headings.text:
Can I use AutoSizer to observe only width or height (not both)? No, but you can memoize your child component so that it only re-renders if width (or height) changes. import { memo } from "react";
import type { SizeProps } from "react-virtualized-auto-sizer";

const MemoizedChildComponent = memo(
 ChildComponent,
 function arePropsEqual(oldProps: SizeProps, newProps: SizeProps) {
 return oldProps.height === newProps.height;
 }
);

text:
AutoSizer measures the available width and height of its parent HTMLElement and passes them as props to a child component. import { AutoSizer, type AutoSizerChildProps } from "react-virtualized-auto-sizer";

function ExampleComponent() {
 return (
 <AutoSizer ChildComponent={ChildComponent} />
 )
}

// Height and width will be undefined for the initial render (or when server rendering)
// You can either set default values (as shown below) or render some sort of placeholder
function ChildComponent({ height = 600, width = 600 }: AutoSizerChildProps) {
 return <div>{width} x {height} pixels</div>;
} The child component is auto-memoized to avoid re-rendering until the size has changed.

The child of an AutoSizer can also be a render prop. import { AutoSizer } from "react-virtualized-auto-sizer";

function ExampleComponent(props: ExampleComponentProps) {
 const [state, setState] = useState("...");

 return (
 <AutoSizer renderProp={
 ({ height = 600, width = 800 }) => {
 // Render prop can access width and height params,
 // as well as the parent component props and state
 }
 } />
 )
} Render props provide the added benefit of being able to reference other values that are in scope.
